{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git diff 8e3009b2 b2fe0321 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/portfolio_projection.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/setup.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/adopt.go'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/adopt.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/adopt.go\nindex ef6fa10f..2f418d84 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/adopt.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/adopt.go\n@@ -19,10 +19,11 @@ import (\n \t\"github.com/harne8/pose-mcp/internal/version\"\n )\n \n-const adoptUsage = \"Usage: pose adopt --list [--json] | pose adopt <capability> [--off | --decline --reason <text> | --defer --reason <text>] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--issuer <name>] [--apply] | pose adopt --request <act-id> [--issuer <name>] [--reason <text>] [--apply]\"\n+const adoptUsage = \"Usage: pose adopt --list [--json] | pose adopt <capability> [--off | --decline --reason <text> | --defer --reason <text>] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--issuer <name>] [--apply] | pose adopt closeout-review-policy --milestone-review-required <never|when-justified|always> --roadmap-review-required <never|when-justified|always> [--apply] | pose adopt --request <act-id> [--issuer <name>] [--reason <text>] [--apply]\"\n \n func cmdAdopt(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n \tid, mode, reason, apply, list, jsonOutput, requestID, issuer := \"\", \"on\", \"\", false, false, false, \"\", \"\"\n+\tmilestoneReview, roadmapReview, closeoutPairGiven := \"\", \"\", false\n \tdate := time.Now().UTC().Format(time.DateOnly)\n \tfor i := 0; i < len(args); i++ {\n \t\tswitch args[i] {\n@@ -38,6 +39,17 @@ func cmdAdopt(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n \t\t\tmode = posemodel.AdoptionDeferred\n \t\tcase \"--apply\":\n \t\t\tapply = true\n+\t\tcase \"--milestone-review-required\", \"--roadmap-review-required\":\n+\t\t\tif i+1 >= len(args) {\n+\t\t\t\treturn usageError(stderr, adoptUsage)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif args[i] == \"--milestone-review-required\" {\n+\t\t\t\tmilestoneReview = args[i+1]\n+\t\t\t} else {\n+\t\t\t\troadmapReview = args[i+1]\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tcloseoutPairGiven = true\n+\t\t\ti++\n \t\tcase \"--date\", \"--reason\", \"--request\", \"--issuer\":\n \t\t\tif i+1 >= len(args) {\n \t\t\t\treturn usageError(stderr, adoptUsage)\n@@ -89,7 +101,7 @@ func cmdAdopt(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n \tif requestID != \"\" {\n \t\t// An answered configuration-review request decides the capability\n \t\t// it asked about (spec pose-update-configuration-review).\n-\t\tif id != \"\" || mode != \"on\" {\n+\t\tif id != \"\" || mode != \"on\" || closeoutPairGiven {\n \t\t\treturn usageError(stderr, adoptUsage)\n \t\t}\n \t\treq, err := loadReviewRequest(root, requestID)\n@@ -132,6 +144,13 @@ func cmdAdopt(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n \tif id == \"\" {\n \t\treturn usageError(stderr, adoptUsage)\n \t}\n+\t// The closeout review pair is set together, only for its own capability,\n+\t// and only to turn it on or change it (spec\n+\t// pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit R6).\n+\tif closeoutPairGiven && (id != \"closeout-review-policy\" || mode != \"on\" || milestoneReview == \"\" || roadmapReview == \"\") {\n+\t\tout.Failure(\"pose adopt: --milestone-review-required and --roadmap-review-required go together, with closeout-review-policy, without --off, --decline or --defer\")\n+\t\treturn 2\n+\t}\n \tentry, known := posemodel.LookupCatalogEntry(id)\n \tif !known {\n \t\tout.Failure(\"pose adopt: unknown capability \" + id + \"; governed capabilities: \" + strings.Join(posemodel.CatalogIDs(), \", \"))\n@@ -186,7 +205,21 @@ func cmdAdopt(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n \t\t\t\treturn 1\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t}\n-\t\tchanges = entry.Adopt(docs, date)\n+\t\tif id == \"closeout-review-policy\" {\n+\t\t\t// Preview shows the rule applied today next to the one proposed.\n+\t\t\t_, milestoneNow, roadmapNow := posemodel.CloseoutReviewPolicyEffective(docs)\n+\t\t\tout.Field(\"adopt.current\", posemodel.MilestoneReviewRequiredKey+\"=\"+milestoneNow+\"; \"+posemodel.RoadmapReviewRequiredKey+\"=\"+roadmapNow)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif closeoutPairGiven {\n+\t\t\tpair, err := posemodel.SetCloseoutReviewPolicy(docs, milestoneReview, roadmapReview)\n+\t\t\tif err != nil {\n+\t\t\t\tout.Failure(\"pose adopt: \" + strings.TrimPrefix(err.Error(), \"pose: \"))\n+\t\t\t\treturn 2\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tchanges = pair\n+\t\t} else {\n+\t\t\tchanges = entry.Adopt(docs, date)\n+\t\t}\n \t}\n \tvar effects []posemodel.AdoptionEffect\n \tif mode == \"on\" && len(changes) > 0 {\n@@ -274,6 +307,11 @@ func adoptGovernedCapabilitiesAtInstallIn(files posemodel.Files, target string,\n \t\treturn\n \t}\n \tfor _, id := range adopted {\n+\t\tif id == \"closeout-review-policy\" {\n+\t\t\t// This one is not turned off: its values change instead.\n+\t\t\tlog(\"capability (adoption): %s from %s — `pose adopt %s --milestone-review-required <never|when-justified|always> --roadmap-review-required <never|when-justified|always> --apply` changes it\", \"capacidade (adoção): %s desde %s — `pose adopt %s --milestone-review-required <never|when-justified|always> --roadmap-review-required <never|when-justified|always> --apply` altera\", id, date, id)\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n \t\tlog(\"capability (adoption): %s from %s — `pose adopt %s --off --apply` turns it off\", \"capacidade (adoção): %s desde %s — `pose adopt %s --off --apply` desliga\", id, date, id)\n \t}\n }\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go\nindex 8944a53d..4e1d0789 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go\n@@ -262,6 +262,7 @@ func runDoctorDiagnostics(locale cliLocale) (root string, findings []doctorFindi\n \t}\n \tadd(\"instance.pose-dir\", \"ok\", text(\".pose/ present\", \".pose/ presente\"), \"\")\n \tdiagnoseProjectState(root, add, text)\n+\tdiagnoseCloseoutReviewPolicy(root, add, text)\n \tdiagnoseReviewContinuity(root, add)\n \n \t// 3. Native engine contract.\n@@ -1574,3 +1575,27 @@ func declaredMCPProjectID(raw []byte) string {\n \tid, _ := doc.MCPServers[\"pose\"].Env[\"POSE_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID\"].(string)\n \treturn id\n }\n+\n+// diagnoseCloseoutReviewPolicy reports open milestones and roadmaps that owe\n+// their own review under the adopted closeout review policy, because of the\n+// policy or of their composition (spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit\n+// R6). It only reports: `pose close` remains the gate.\n+func diagnoseCloseoutReviewPolicy(root string, add func(string, string, string, string), text func(string, string) string) {\n+\tstore := posemodel.Store{Root: root}\n+\tpolicy, err := store.GetReviewPolicy()\n+\tif err != nil || !policy.CloseoutReviewAdopted() {\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\towing, err := store.CloseoutReviewsOwed()\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tadd(\"closeout-review.owed\", \"warn\", fmt.Sprintf(text(\"open scopes owing a closeout review could not be listed: %v\", \"escopos abertos que devem revisão de fechamento não puderam ser listados: %v\"), err), text(\"run `pose closeout-check <scope>` for each open milestone and roadmap\", \"rode `pose closeout-check <escopo>` para cada milestone e roadmap aberto\"))\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tif len(owing) == 0 {\n+\t\tadd(\"closeout-review.owed\", \"ok\", fmt.Sprintf(text(\"no open scope owes a review it lacks (milestone_review_required=%s, roadmap_review_required=%s)\", \"nenhum escopo aberto deve uma revisão que não tem (milestone_review_required=%s, roadmap_review_required=%s)\"), policy.MilestoneReviewRequired, policy.RoadmapReviewRequired), \"\")\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, item := range owing {\n+\t\tadd(\"closeout-review.owed\", \"warn\", fmt.Sprintf(text(\"%s owes its own review: %s=%s, %s; previous rule %s\", \"%s deve revisão própria: %s=%s, %s; regra anterior %s\"), item.Scope, item.Decision.PolicyKey, item.Decision.PolicyValue, item.Decision.Reason, item.Previous), item.Action)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/portfolio_projection.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/portfolio_projection.go\nindex 67220020..48d1dd28 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/portfolio_projection.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/portfolio_projection.go\n@@ -174,6 +174,11 @@ func buildPortfolioProjection(now time.Time, knownProjects map[string]string, ma\n \t\t\t\t\tres.Reason = resolved.State\n \t\t\t\t} else {\n \t\t\t\t\tres.Blocking = resolved.Status != \"done\"\n+\t\t\t\t\t// A milestone or roadmap of a project that adopted the\n+\t\t\t\t\t// closeout review policy is done only once closed.\n+\t\t\t\t\tif closed, why := store.AggregateDependencyClosed(resolver, project, resolved); !res.Blocking && !closed {\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tres.Blocking, res.Reason = true, why\n+\t\t\t\t\t}\n \t\t\t\t\tif reason := resolver.ValidateGraph(project, dep); reason != \"\" {\n \t\t\t\t\t\tres.Blocking, res.Reason = true, reason\n \t\t\t\t\t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/setup.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/setup.go\nindex 9d48840c..501849ed 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/setup.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/setup.go\n@@ -65,10 +65,22 @@ type setupPlan struct {\n \tNeedsSetup      []posemodel.CapabilityState `json:\"needs_setup\"`\n \tAvailable       []string                    `json:\"available\"`\n \tOnboarding      string                      `json:\"onboarding_spec,omitempty\"`\n+\tCloseoutReview  setupCloseoutReview         `json:\"closeout_review\"`\n \tSteps           []setupStep                 `json:\"steps\"`\n \tNext            *setupStep                  `json:\"next,omitempty\"`\n }\n \n+// setupCloseoutReview shows the closeout review rule in force and the pair an\n+// adoption would write (spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit R6).\n+type setupCloseoutReview struct {\n+\tAdopted           bool   `json:\"adopted\"`\n+\tMilestone         string `json:\"milestone_review_required\"`\n+\tRoadmap           string `json:\"roadmap_review_required\"`\n+\tProposedMilestone string `json:\"proposed_milestone_review_required,omitempty\"`\n+\tProposedRoadmap   string `json:\"proposed_roadmap_review_required,omitempty\"`\n+\tCommand           string `json:\"command\"`\n+}\n+\n // candidateKeyFile returns the user's public key POSE would suggest\n // registering, preferring a security key.\n func candidateKeyFile() string {\n@@ -135,6 +147,14 @@ func buildSetupPlan(root string) (setupPlan, error) {\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn plan, err\n \t}\n+\tif docs, err := posemodel.LoadPolicyDocs(root); err == nil {\n+\t\tadopted, milestone, roadmap := posemodel.CloseoutReviewPolicyEffective(docs)\n+\t\tplan.CloseoutReview = setupCloseoutReview{Adopted: adopted, Milestone: milestone, Roadmap: roadmap,\n+\t\t\tCommand: \"pose adopt closeout-review-policy --milestone-review-required <never|when-justified|always> --roadmap-review-required <never|when-justified|always> --apply\"}\n+\t\tif !adopted {\n+\t\t\tplan.CloseoutReview.ProposedMilestone, plan.CloseoutReview.ProposedRoadmap = posemodel.CloseoutReviewNever, posemodel.CloseoutReviewNever\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n \tisNew := map[string]bool{}\n \tfor _, state := range review {\n \t\tisNew[state.ID] = true\n@@ -396,6 +416,14 @@ func renderSetupPlan(rawField func(string, string), section func(string), plan s\n \tfor _, state := range plan.NeedsSetup {\n \t\tfield(\"setup.needs_setup.\"+state.ID, state.Missing)\n \t}\n+\tif closeout := plan.CloseoutReview; closeout.Milestone != \"\" {\n+\t\tline := \"milestone_review_required=\" + closeout.Milestone + \"; roadmap_review_required=\" + closeout.Roadmap\n+\t\tif !closeout.Adopted {\n+\t\t\tline += \" — adopting proposes milestone_review_required=\" + closeout.ProposedMilestone + \", roadmap_review_required=\" + closeout.ProposedRoadmap\n+\t\t}\n+\t\trawField(\"setup.closeout_review\", line)\n+\t\trawField(\"setup.closeout_review.command\", closeout.Command)\n+\t}\n \tif len(plan.Available) > 0 {\n \t\tsort.Strings(plan.Available)\n \t\tfield(\"setup.available\", strings.Join(plan.Available, \", \")+\" — off; `pose adopt --list` explains each\")\n@@ -489,7 +517,19 @@ func runSetupInteractive(root string, plan setupPlan, in *bufio.Reader, stdout,\n \t\t\tanswer := strings.ToLower(ask(step.Summary + \"\\n  [a]dopt, [d]ecline, [l]ater (defer), [s]kip? \"))\n \t\t\tswitch answer {\n \t\t\tcase \"a\", \"adopt\":\n-\t\t\t\tif code := cmdAdopt(root, []string{step.capability, \"--apply\"}, stdout, stderr); code != 0 {\n+\t\t\t\targs := []string{step.capability, \"--apply\"}\n+\t\t\t\tif step.capability == \"closeout-review-policy\" {\n+\t\t\t\t\t// The pair is chosen here and written by the same operation.\n+\t\t\t\t\tchoose := func(key string) string {\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tvalue := strings.TrimSpace(ask(\"  \" + key + \" [never|when-justified|always] (never)? \"))\n+\t\t\t\t\t\tif value == \"\" {\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t\tvalue = posemodel.CloseoutReviewNever\n+\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t\t\t\treturn value\n+\t\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t\t\targs = []string{step.capability, \"--milestone-review-required\", choose(\"milestone_review_required\"), \"--roadmap-review-required\", choose(\"roadmap_review_required\"), \"--apply\"}\n+\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t\tif code := cmdAdopt(root, args, stdout, stderr); code != 0 {\n \t\t\t\t\treturn code\n \t\t\t\t}\n \t\t\t\tdecided = true\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go\nindex bd17f7a4..aada4858 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go\n@@ -56,6 +56,10 @@ type Store struct {\n \tRoot               string // project root containing .pose/\n \tFederatedProjectID string\n \tFederatedResolver  *ArtifactResolver\n+\t// closeoutChain is the chain of local aggregate scopes whose terminal\n+\t// verification is asking for this one, through their dependency edges:\n+\t// a scope already in it is a cycle and is not proven closed.\n+\tcloseoutChain []string\n \t// specs, when set, is the spec listing of one operation, read once\n \t// (spec pose-attention-within-a-second). Nil outside such an operation.\n \tspecs *specSnapshot\n@@ -67,6 +71,10 @@ type Store struct {\n \t// the disk, a preview reads its staged view. A store built from this one\n \t// carries it on.\n \tFS Files\n+\t// planWithoutCloseoutGate builds a review plan without asking the\n+\t// closeout review gate, for the gate's own question about the plan's\n+\t// effective independence (spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit).\n+\tplanWithoutCloseoutGate bool\n }\n \n // fsys is the store's filesystem.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md .pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md .pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md'","aggregated_output":"---\ntype: decision-log\nslug: adr-component-aware-review-plans-review\nowner: @pose-maintainers\nsensitivity: public-internal\ncreated_at: 2026-08-13\nlast_reviewed_at: 2026-08-13\nexpires_at: 2026-11-11\nsource_refs:\n  spec: \"pose-component-aware-review-plans\"\n  workflow: \"feature\"\n  commands: [\"pose assess discover --component pose-mcp/internal/pose\", \"pose lint-spec pose-component-aware-review-plans --ready-check\"]\n  external_sources: []  # [{url: \"\", accessed_at: \"YYYY-MM-DD\"}]\n---\n\n# decision-log: adr-component-aware-review-plans-review\n\n## Context\n\nPOSE 1.0 binds immutable review attempts to a scope-kind profile but does not\ncompose criteria or tool guidance from the mapped components. The implementation\nintroduces a public schema-v2 policy/profile contract, CLI/MCP projections and a\nnew plan digest, so the design needs an explicit future-review trigger.\n\n## Current state\n\nADR `2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans` is accepted. It chooses\ntyped one-level overlays, deterministic union into one effective plan, a closed\nnative-tool catalog and additive schema-v1 compatibility. Implementation is\ntracked by `pose-component-aware-review-plans`.\n\n## Next checks\n\n- Verify frontend, backend and multi-component golden plans.\n- Verify command/path/symlink/selector negative cases.\n- Verify CLI/MCP schema parity and scaffold distribution.\n- Review production false-staleness before 2026-11-11.\n\n## Risks\n\nComponent maps can be stale and overlay composition can make unrelated metadata\ninvalidate approvals. Keep mapping provenance visible, include only consumed\ninputs in the digest and reject conflicts instead of selecting heuristically.\n\n## Next owner\n\n`@pose-maintainers`.\n\n## References\n\n- `spec:pose-component-aware-review-plans`\n- `adr:2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans`\n- https://github.com/oseiaspereira88/pose/issues/13 (accessed 2026-08-13)\n---\ntype: decision-log\nslug: adr-sealed-review-bundles-review\nowner: @pose-maintainers\nsensitivity: public-internal\ncreated_at: 2026-08-13\nlast_reviewed_at: 2026-08-13\nexpires_at: 2026-11-11\nsource_refs:\n  spec: \"pose-review-bundle-convergence\"\n  workflow: \"feature\"\n  commands: [\"pose lint-spec pose-review-bundle-convergence --ready-check\", \"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --report --report-task review-bundle-convergence\"]\n  external_sources: []\n---\n\n# decision-log: adr-sealed-review-bundles-review\n\n## Context\n\nThe current full-body review scope digest lets closeout bookkeeping alter the\nsubject that was just approved. Component-aware review also exposed transient\nprovider merge provenance and excessive full-plan rereview. The proposed ADR\nseparates a canonical sealed bundle from its attestation and makes POSE the\noffline verifier while an optional Conductor workflow owns orchestration.\n\n## Current state\n\nADR `2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations` is accepted. The core,\nCLI, read-only MCP, schemas, opt-in migration, scoped provenance bridge,\nEnglish/pt-BR distribution and fresh-repository convergence smoke are\nimplemented under `pose-review-bundle-convergence`.\n\n## Next checks\n\n- Prove `prepare -> validate -> seal -> review -> attest -> close` converges\n  without a second bundle or review.\n- Prove lifecycle, state, assessment, report and attestation mutations do not\n  change the sealed bundle.\n- Prove every governed semantic, source, policy and required-evidence mutation\n  supersedes the affected bundle.\n- Verify synthetic merge/squash subjects by patch and tree/content digests.\n- Verify policy-bounded targeted criterion reuse and complete final projection.\n- Verify a new delivery target cannot stale unrelated closed specs and that no\n  historical evidence must be regenerated to recover the strict gate.\n- Verify repeated mapping warnings and inactive completion tools are grouped in\n  human output while canonical JSON retains complete provenance.\n- Verify offline flow, installed-binary parity and schema-v1/v2 migration before\n  promoting the feature from preview.\n\n## Risks\n\nSemantic projection may omit a meaningful input or retain an operational input,\ncausing false freshness or false staleness. Keep unknown paths fail-closed,\nrequire include/exclude golden fixtures and review production deltas after the\nfirst opt-in release. Criterion reuse may miss cross-cutting effects; disable it\nfor high-criticality profiles until sliced-input evidence proves safe.\n\n## Next owner\n\n`@pose-maintainers`.\n\n## References\n\n- `spec:pose-review-bundle-convergence`\n- `adr:2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations`\n- `adr:2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans`\n- `knowledge:pr15-component-aware-review-provenance`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
